{
  "A short text with an icon or an avatar before it: a filter to turn on, a choice among a few, or something picked that can be removed. A group selects one or several and moves between them with the arrow keys.": "",
  "Looks and states": "",
  "Choosing in a group": "",
  "`selection` makes the chips choices; `value` holds their values and `onValueChanged` tells a change.": "",
  "Removing": "",
  "A removable chip only asks: `onRemove` is where your list loses the item, and the group follows the list.": "",
  "Presses the chip: turns a selectable one on or off, selects one in a group.": "",
  "Asks to remove a removable chip.": "",
  "In a group: move between the chips. Tab stops once on the group, at the chip focused last.": "",
  "A button with `aria-pressed`.": "",
  "The group is a `listbox` (`aria-multiselectable` for several), each chip an `option` with `aria-selected`.": "",
  "The remove button is named “Remove Ada” in the kit language; the keyboard reaches it through Delete on the chip.": "",
  "Out of the Tab order and marked `aria-disabled`.": "",
  "The remove button’s name is the kit text `removeItem` (“Remove {text}”) and changes with the kit language (`uiLocale`).": "",
  "The chip. `data-size`, `data-variant`, `data-selected`, `data-pressable`, `data-removable`, `data-lead`, `data-check`, `data-disabled`.": "",
  "What stands before the text.": "",
  "The text, and the remove button.": "",
  "The group. `data-wrap`.": "",
  "Unit: the chip, filled at rest, then `outline`, each tone filled and outlined (`accent` … `danger`, `outline-*`), `selected`, `hover`, `pressed`, `focus`, `disabled`.": "",
  "Units: the icon or check mark; the remove button (`hover`, `pressed`).": "",
  "The chip, its text and its spaces, per size.": "",
  "What stands before and after the text, per size. An avatar and the remove button sit as far in from the edge as from the top and bottom.": "",
  "The look a chip takes when none is given; whether a selected chip shows a check mark (Material).": "",
  "The space between chips.": "",
  "Chip props": "",
  "its text": "",
  "What it stands for in a group’s value.": "",
  "An icon before the text: an image address, an element or a component.": "",
  "An avatar before the text (its props; the chip sets its size).": "",
  "Pressed, it turns on and off (a filter). In a group that selects, the group decides.": "",
  "Whether it is on.": "",
  "It can be pressed like a button (`onclick`).": "",
  "A remove button after the text; it and Delete / Backspace raise `onRemove`.": "",
  "`filled`, `outline`. Material draws chips outlined, the other languages filled.": "",
  "`standard`, `accent`, `info`, `success`, `caution`, `danger`; a selected chip shows the selection instead.": "",
  "Chip events": "",
  "The user asked to remove it (`byKeyboard`); removing it is yours to do.": "",
  "It was turned on or off (`selected`), by the user or by code (`byUser`).": "",
  "Chip properties": "",
  "The avatar before the text, when it has one.": "",
  "Chip methods": "",
  "Asks for it to be removed, as its remove button does (raises `onRemove`).": "",
  "ChipGroup props": "",
  "The selected chip’s value (`single`), or an array of the selected ones’ values (`multiple`). A change gives a new array. Two-way with `x-model`.": "",
  "`false` keeps the chips on one line that scrolls.": "",
  "What screen readers call the group (“Diet”).": "",
  "ChipGroup events, properties and methods": "",
  "The chips in it, in order, from JSX lists too.": "",
  "Whether the chip of `value` is selected.": ""
